  },
  "disclosure": "This app is optimised for Jamaican statement data. Some merchant classifications come from a shared Jamaica focused knowledge base and are refined by your own corrections, which always take priority.",
  "merchants": {
    "file": "jamaica-merchants.json",
    "note": "When a statement is imported, each descriptor is first checked against this researched merchant list (name, aliases, category, brand/group, parent, country, confidence). If nothing matches, the existing category rules below decide. A person's own corrections always win over both."
  },
  "bankDescriptorCleanup": {
    "note": "Statement-format facts about how a bank counterparty text is formatted - never application logic, never a category decision. Applied, in order, to every bank-ledger counterparty description before display, after the existing header-fragment peel. Includes structural removal of a sending bank's SWIFT/BIC code (matched by the ISO 9362 8- or 11-character shape for the correspondent countries that route these wires, not one hardcoded country) and the trailing payment-reference suffix (any opaque alphanumeric trace/RTGS/ACH token that contains a digit, not only digit-led ones) that ride along in third-party transfer narratives.",
    "rules": [
      {
        "pattern": "^\\*(?:bns\\s+)?",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "",
        "note": "ABM/POS terminal marker: a leading '*BNS ' or bare '*' before the real merchant name."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\s+for\\s+\\d{1,2}[A-Za-z]{3}\\d{2}\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "",
        "note": "Statement processing-date suffix (' For 29Dec25'), confirmed optional - the same merchant appears both with and without it."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\s+jm\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "",
        "note": "Trailing standalone country code, never glued onto another word."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\bf\\s+inan\\.?\\s+centre\\b",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "Financial Centre",
        "note": "Wrapped 'Constant Spring Financial Centre' split by a PDF column boundary."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\b(Salary|Payroll)\\s+(Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Oct|Nov|Dec)(?=,\\s*Payroll\\b)",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "$1",
        "note": "Payroll ACH narratives commonly embed the pay-period month (a documented Nacha PAYROLL-description convention, not specific to any one employer). Strips it so recurring salary deposits from the same employer group under one counterparty across every pay period instead of splitting into one group per month."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\bSalary,\\s*Payroll\\b\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "Salary",
        "note": "The no-month variant of the Nacha PAYROLL convention: a narrative ending 'Salary, Payroll' (with no pay-period month between them, so the month-stripping rule above does not fire) carries a redundant trailing ', Payroll' descriptor after the salary label. Collapses it to a single 'Salary' so the employer's salary deposits read cleanly and group as one counterparty, matching the month-embedded variant's own result."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "(Salary|Payroll)\\w*.*?Payroll\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "Salary",
        "note": "Some payroll deposits from the same employer carry an inline pay-period reference that varies month to month (for example 'Salary1 Oc, Payroll' or 'Payroll Ma, Payroll'), which the earlier fixed-shape rules do not catch. Left alone, each variant becomes its own counterparty and one salary stream splits into several, so those months read as missed deposits when the salary genuinely arrived. Collapses any salary/payroll label followed by trailing pay-period text and a closing 'Payroll' back to a single 'Salary', so every pay period groups under one counterparty. End-anchored, so a plain '...Salary' with no trailing 'Payroll' is never touched."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "(Salary|Payroll)\\w*.*?Payroll\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "Salary",
        "note": "Some payroll deposits from the same employer carry an inline pay-period reference that varies month to month (for example 'Salary1 Oc, Payroll' or 'Payroll Ma, Payroll'), which the earlier fixed-shape rules do not catch. Left alone, each variant becomes its own counterparty and one salary stream splits into several, so those months read as missed deposits when the salary genuinely arrived. Collapses any salary/payroll label followed by trailing pay-period text and a closing 'Payroll' back to a single 'Salary', so every pay period groups under one counterparty. End-anchored, so a plain '...Salary' with no trailing 'Payroll' is never touched."
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\s+(Citibank(\\s*N\\.?A\\.?)?|JPMorgan\\s*Chase(\\s*Bank)?(\\s*N\\.?A\\.?)?|Chase\\s*Bank|Bank\\s*of\\s*New\\s*York\\s*Mellon|BNY\\s*Mellon|HSBC(\\s*Bank)?(\\s*USA)?|Barclays(\\s*Bank)?|Standard\\s*Chartered(\\s*Bank)?|Deutsche\\s*Bank(\\s*Trust)?|BNP\\s*Paribas|Wells\\s*Fargo(\\s*Bank)?|Bank\\s*of\\s*America)\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "",
        "note": "International USD/GBP wires commonly append the correspondent/clearing bank used to route the payment after the true beneficiary name. This list covers the major named global USD/GBP correspondents, not any single merchant, so a wire beneficiary groups correctly with that same beneficiary's other transactions regardless of which correspondent bank handled clearing."
      },
      {
        "pattern": ",\\s*[A-Z]{4}[A-Z]{2}[A-Z0-9]{2}(?:[A-Z0-9]{3})?(?=\\s*,\\s*\\d)",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": ""
      },
      {
        "pattern": "\\bthird\\s+party\\s+trf\\s+fee\\b",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": "Third Party Transfer Fee"
      },
      {
        "pattern": "(?:\\s*,\\s*(?=[A-Z0-9]*\\d)[A-Z0-9]{8,})+\\s*$",
        "flags": "i",
        "replacement": ""
      }
    ]
  },
  "accountCategoryRoutes": {
    "note": "Account-type routing for categories the shared register cannot get right for both ledgers. A term can mean different things depending on which statement it appears on: 'insurance premium' on a CARD is the card issuer's own insurance fee (Fees & Interest), while the same words on a BANK statement are the person paying their insurer (Insurance). Applied only AFTER the shared engine has produced `from`, and only for the named profile, so the card ledger is untouched and no rule is invented for a category the engine did not already choose. These change the LABEL a row carries, never the amount and never which plan group it lands in when both categories share one group.",
    "bank": [
      { "match": "INSURANCE PREMIUM", "from": "Fees & Interest", "to": "Insurance" }
    ]
  },
  "planBands": {
    "note": "The Plan tab's conscious-spending groups. Every spending category belongs to exactly one group, and each group carries a target share of a normal month's take-home. defaults are the starting split (60/20/20), a reference point a person tunes - never a pass mark and never a grade. seed places only the categories whose group is NOT a judgement call; everything in seed.ask is a real decision and is put to the person rather than guessed. A category's group is decided by OBLIGATION, not by rhythm: a bill you must pay is fixed, while dining or entertainment is discretionary spending however regularly it recurs. Recurrence is therefore never used to infer a group. Detected recurring standing debits count as fixed because a direct debit is a contractual obligation, not merely a repeated one.",
    "groups": [
      { "key": "fixed", "label": "Fixed expenses", "meaning": "money you are obliged to pay" },
      { "key": "setAside", "label": "Savings & investments", "meaning": "money moving toward the future" },
      { "key": "free", "label": "Discretionary spending", "meaning": "money you choose how to spend" }
    ],
    "defaults": { "fixed": 60, "setAside": 20, "free": 20 },
    "seed": {
      "fixed": [
        "Utilities",
        "Telecom",
        "Insurance",
        "Loan Repayment",
        "Government & Tax",
        "Fees & Interest"
      ],
      "setAside": [],
      "free": [
        "Dining & Takeout",
        "Entertainment & Recreation",
        "Subscriptions",
        "Online Shopping",
        "Retail & Department",
        "Hotels & Travel"
      ],
      "ask": [
        "Groceries",
        "Fuel & Transport",
        "Auto & Vehicle",
        "Pharmacy & Health",
        "Home & Services",
        "Courier & Shipping",
        "Banking & Transfers"
      ]
    }
  },
  "bankMovementKinds": {
    "note": "Bank-native movement rules used by the Plan tab to distinguish money set aside from neutral transfers and to coarsen bank categories. A row's kind is decided in bank-analysis.js bankMovementKind(): setAsideRules first, then own-account/round-trip, cash deposit, household, resolved category, statement type, and finally direction.",
    "setAsideRules": [
      { "match": "INVESTMENT", "label": "Investment account", "investment": true },
      { "match": "BROKERAGE", "label": "Brokerage account", "investment": true },
      { "match": "MUTUAL FUND", "label": "Mutual fund", "investment": true },
      { "match": "UNIT TRUST", "label": "Unit trust", "investment": true },
      { "match": "FIXED DEPOSIT", "label": "Fixed deposit" },
      { "match": "PENSION", "label": "Pension" },
      { "match": "RETIREMENT", "label": "Retirement account" },
      { "match": "SINKING FUND", "label": "Sinking fund" }
    ],
    "categoryToKind": {
      "Insurance": "bill",
      "Banking & Transfers": "bill",
      "Loan Repayment": "bill",
      "Utilities": "bill",
      "Telecom": "bill",
      "Government & Tax": "tax"
    },
    "typeRules": [
      { "match": "SPECIAL SERVICE CHARGE", "kind": "fees" },
      { "match": "SERVICE CHARGE", "kind": "fees" },
      { "match": "TRANSACTIONAL FEE", "kind": "fees" },
      { "match": "DEBIT INTEREST", "kind": "fees" },
      { "match": "WITHHOLDING TAX", "kind": "tax" },
      { "match": "GOVT TAX", "kind": "tax" },
      { "match": "GCT", "kind": "tax" },
      { "match": "ABM WITHDRAWAL", "kind": "cash-withdrawal" },
      { "match": "ABM DEPOSIT", "kind": "cash-deposit" },
      { "match": "INTEREST PAYMENT", "kind": "income" },
      { "match": "SCOTIA DIRECT CREDIT", "kind": "income" },
      { "match": "SALARY", "kind": "income" },
      { "match": "PAYROLL", "kind": "income" },
      { "match": "ELECTRONIC DATA DEBIT", "kind": "bill" },
      { "match": "ELECTRONIC DEBIT", "kind": "bill" },
      { "match": "PC-BILL PAYMENT", "kind": "bill" }
    ]
  },
